  "id": "COMPOUND:3827 - PROTEIN:1026",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that p-Coumaric acid may interact with Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1 through multiple distinct pathways. The primary mechanism involves p-Coumaric acid targeting DNA gyrase subunit B, which is a key component of the DNA replication machinery. This interaction is supported by the presence of a target-specific inhibitor, (1S,2S,3S,5As,10Ar)-1,10A-Dihydroxy-6'-Methoxy-3-(2-Methylprop-1-Enyl)Spiro[1,3,5A,6,7,8-Hexahydrodipyrrolo[1,2-D:1',2'-F]Pyrazine-2,2'-1H-Indole]-3',5,10-Trione, which is a known inhibitor of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. Additionally, p-Coumaric acid is also shown to target another protein, Sodium- and chloride-dependent GABA transporter 1, which is further inhibited by Npc11947, another protein that targets Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1. These findings collectively indicate that p-Coumaric acid may exert its effects on Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1 through different molecular pathways, highlighting the complexity of the relationship between this compound and the target protein. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, suggesting a potential role for p-Coumaric acid in modulating the activity of Cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 1 through various molecular mechanisms.",
